{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"a95015031a9cdb42","x":-5760,"y":7040,"width":2760,"height":1200,"type":"group","label":"Data Patterns"},
		{"id":"cb6b6b31cce62180","type":"text","text":"### Financial Planning and Analysis. \n\n\n\n\n### Accounting system hierarchy.\n\n#### 1. Chart of accounts. - Master Account\n\n*Purpose*: **Defines what account exist.**\n- Authoritative list of all account codes\n- Contains account attributes:\n    - Account number\n    - Account name\n    - Account type (Asset, Liability, Equity, Revenue, Expense)\n    - Reporting classification\n- Changes infrequently\n- No balances, no transactions\n\n**Conclusion:**  \nThe **Chart of Accounts is the master reference** used by all other financial artifacts.\n\n#### 2. General Ledger - Transaction System. \n\n**Role:** System of record for postings  \n**Purpose:** Records _how accounts are used_\n- Stores journal entries\n- References accounts defined in the CoA\n- Maintains running balances by account and period\n- Cannot exist without the CoA\n**Dependency:**  \nGL → depends on → CoA\n\n#### 3. Trail balance - Derived Snapshot\n\n**Role:** Reporting artifact  \n**Purpose:** Summarizes _financial position at a point in time_\n\n- Aggregated balances per account\n- Derived from the General Ledger\n- Used for validation and financial reporting\n- Fully dependent on GL (and indirectly CoA)\n\n**Dependency:**  \nTrial Balance → derived from → GL → based on → CoA","x":-12761,"y":6060,"width":960,"height":1100},
		{"id":"14033958a010edb9","type":"text","text":"## Real-World Scenario: Small Retail Store\n\n**Business:** ABC Electronics  \n**Event:** Business starts operations and sells goods during January\n\n---\n\n## 1️⃣ Chart of Accounts (CoA) — _Set up BEFORE business starts_\n\nThis is created **once**, before any transaction happens.\n\n> Think of CoA as the **menu of allowed accounts** in the system.\n\n|Account Code|Account Name|Type|Used for|\n|---|---|---|---|\n|1010|Cash|Asset|Cash in hand / bank|\n|1020|Accounts Receivable|Asset|Customer dues|\n|2010|Accounts Payable|Liability|Vendor dues|\n|3010|Owner Capital|Equity|Owner investment|\n|4010|Sales Revenue|Revenue|Sales income|\n|5010|Operating Expenses|Expense|Rent, utilities, etc.|\n\n**Real life meaning:**  \nThese accounts must exist **before** anyone can record money movement.\n\n---\n\n## 2️⃣ General Ledger (GL) — _Day-to-day real transactions_\n\nNow the business starts operating.\n\n---\n\n### 📌 Transaction 1: Owner invests money\n\n**Date:** Jan 1  \n**Real life:** Owner deposits ₹100,000 into business bank account.\n\n|Account|Debit|Credit|\n|---|---|---|\n|Cash (1010)|100,000||\n|Owner Capital (3010)||100,000|\n\n**Why?**\n\n- Cash increases → Debit\n    \n- Owner’s equity increases → Credit\n    \n\n---\n\n### 📌 Transaction 2: Sale made on credit\n\n**Date:** Jan 5  \n**Real life:** Goods sold worth ₹40,000; customer will pay later.\n\n|Account|Debit|Credit|\n|---|---|---|\n|Accounts Receivable (1020)|40,000||\n|Sales Revenue (4010)||40,000|\n\n**Why?**\n\n- Customer owes money → Asset increases\n    \n- Revenue earned → Credit\n    \n\n---\n\n### 📌 Transaction 3: Paid shop rent\n\n**Date:** Jan 10  \n**Real life:** Paid ₹15,000 rent in cash.\n\n|Account|Debit|Credit|\n|---|---|---|\n|Operating Expenses (5010)|15,000||\n|Cash (1010)||15,000|\n\n**Why?**\n\n- Expense increases → Debit\n    \n- Cash decreases → Credit\n    \n\n---\n\n### 📘 General Ledger (System View)\n\n|Date|Account Code|Account Name|Debit|Credit|\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n|Jan 1|1010|Cash|100,000||\n|Jan 1|3010|Owner Capital||100,000|\n|Jan 5|1020|Accounts Receivable|40,000||\n|Jan 5|4010|Sales Revenue||40,000|\n|Jan 10|5010|Operating Expenses|15,000||\n|Jan 10|1010|Cash||15,000|\n\nThis **is the General Ledger**:  \nEvery financial event, recorded line by line, referencing the CoA.\n\n---\n\n## 3️⃣ Trial Balance — _End-of-month real report_\n\nAt the end of January, the accountant runs **Trial Balance**.\n\n> Think of Trial Balance as **“Where does the business stand today?”**\n\n### Trial Balance as of Jan 31\n\n|Account|Debit (₹)|Credit (₹)|\n|---|---|---|\n|Cash|85,000||\n|Accounts Receivable|40,000||\n|Owner Capital||100,000|\n|Sales Revenue||40,000|\n|Operating Expenses|15,000||\n|**Total**|**140,000**|**140,000**|","x":-5160,"y":3320,"width":1520,"height":2866},
		{"id":"990b87ce0cc89cac","type":"text","text":"| Artifact              | Type             | Master? | Description                       |\n| --------------------- | ---------------- | ------- | --------------------------------- |\n| **Chart of Accounts** | Master data      | **Yes** | Defines all valid accounts        |\n| General Ledger        | Transactional    | No      | Records postings against accounts |\n| Trial Balance         | Derived / Report | No      | Aggregated balances for a period  |","x":-2960,"y":1360,"width":680,"height":180},
		{"id":"7b7384e2c25a40bd","type":"text","text":"## Trail Balance\n\n|                 |             |                |               |                    |               |                      |             |                      |           |           |      |           |              |             |\n| --------------- | ----------- | -------------- | ------------- | ------------------ | ------------- | -------------------- | ----------- | -------------------- | --------- | --------- | ---- | --------- | ------------ | ----------- |\n| _Account Number | _Subsidiary | _Subsidiary ID | _3 Months Ago | _Formula (Numeric) | _2 Months Ago | _Formula (Numeric).1 | _Last Month | _Formula (Numeric).2 | _Event ID | _Opponent | _Day | _Activity | _Activity ID | _Department |\n\n## General Ledger\n|                      |                 |               |         |                            |       |             |                |                  |                |                 |       |          |                  |       |              |       |         |             |                  |                      |       |        |                    |           |      |           |                       |                   |\n| -------------------- | --------------- | ------------- | ------- | -------------------------- | ----- | ----------- | -------------- | ---------------- | -------------- | --------------- | ----- | -------- | ---------------- | ----- | ------------ | ----- | ------- | ----------- | ---------------- | -------------------- | ----- | ------ | ------------------ | --------- | ---- | --------- | --------------------- | ----------------- |\n| _Account Description | _Account Number | _Account Type | _Amount | _Amount (Foreign Currency) | _Date | _Department | _Department ID | _Document Number | _Exchange Rate | _Invoice Number | _Item | _Line ID | _Line Unique Key | _Memo | _Memo (Main) | _Name | _Period | _Subsidiary | _Subsidiary Name | _Subsidiary Currency | _Type | _Event | _Event External ID | _Opponent | _Day | _Activity | _Activity External ID | _ramp_receipt_url |\n\n## COA\n\n|      |              |               |              |           |      |            |              |\n| ---- | ------------ | ------------- | ------------ | --------- | ---- | ---------- | ------------ |\n| _dim | _member_name | _member_alias | _parent_name | _operator | _cmd | _member_id | _external_id |","x":-13940,"y":7520,"width":3400,"height":460},
		{"id":"a8001d4ed9ae80e2","x":-12400,"y":8600,"width":1120,"height":2280,"type":"text","text":"## General Ledger/ Transaction File"},
		{"id":"d9ad9aebed22187e","type":"text","text":"## Chart of Accounts: \n\n* It's a dimension or master table. \n* It cannot be rolled up\n* Predefined, differs client to client\n* It defines what account exists and how they are organized. \n\n\n\n## Column details:\n\n1. **dim**: The dimension namespace this row belongs to.\n\t1. It defines what kind of member it is. \n\t2. Identifies **which logical dimension** this row belongs to (e.g., Account, Cost Center, Product).\n\t3. example: dim = \"ACCOUNT\"\n\t4. This row represents a General Ledger account, not a department or product\n2. member_id: \n\t1. A **system-generated, immutable internal identifier** for the account.\n\t2. Why it exists\n\t\t1. Names change\n\t\t2. Account numbers can change\n\t\t3. Internal IDs **must never change**\n\t3. Something like a true primary key\n\t4. This is the system’s permanent identity for the Sales Revenue account\n3. external_id:\n\t1. The **business account number** used by accountants and ERP systems.\n\t2. Why it exists\n\t\t1. This is the **natural key** referenced by:\n\t\t\t1.  General Ledger\n\t\t\t2. Trial Balance\n\t\t\t3. Financial reports\n\t\t2. Real-time example external_id = \"4000\"\n\t\t3. Account 4000 = Sales Revenue in the accounting system.\n4. member_name: \n\t1. The official, human-readable name of the account.\n\t2. Why it exists\n\t\t1. Reporting\n\t\t2. Readability\n\t\t3. Financial statements\n\t3. Not guaranteed to be unique.\n\t4. Real-time example\n\t\t1. member_name = \"Sales Revenue\"\n\t5. This account records income earned from selling goods or services\n5. member_alias:\n\t1. An **alternate or secondary name** for the same account\n\t2. Why it exists\n\t\t1. Used when:\n\t\t\t1. Multiple naming standards exist\n\t\t\t2. ERP migrations happen\n\t\t\t3. Short codes are preferred\n\t\t2. Real time example:\n\t\t\t1. member_alias = \"REV_SALES\"\n\t3. Internal shorthand or legacy name for Sales Revenue\n6. parent_name:\n\t1. The **parent node in the account hierarchy** that this account rolls up to.\n\t2. Why it exists\n\t\t1. Supports:\n\t\t\t1. Financial statement structure\n\t\t\t2. Hierarchical rollups\n\t\t\t\t1. Aggregation logic\n\t3. Real-time example `parent_name = \"Revenue\"`\n\t4. Meaning hierarchy: `Revenue  └── Sales Revenue`\n7. operator\n\t1. Specifies **how the account behaves mathematically** during aggregation.\n\t2. Some accounts **subtract** from totals instead of adding.\n\t3. Discounts reduce total revenue when rolled up\n8. cmd\n\t1. A **semantic instruction or classification flag** that tells systems how to treat the account.\n\t2. cmd = \"INCULDE_IN_BS\"\n\t\t1. Include this account in the Balance Sheet\n\n\n\n\n# Complete Real-World Example Row:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"dim\": \"ACCOUNT\",\n  \"member_id\": \"acc_000145\",\n  \"external_id\": \"4000\",\n  \"member_name\": \"Sales Revenue\",\n  \"member_alias\": \"REV_SALES\",\n  \"parent_name\": \"Revenue\",\n  \"operator\": \"+\",\n  \"cmd\": \"INCLUDE_IN_PL\"\n}\n```\n\n### Business interpretation\n\n> “Account 4000 is Sales Revenue, a child of Revenue, adds positively to totals, and appears in the P&L.”","x":-13940,"y":8600,"width":1080,"height":2280},
		{"id":"3b896b52536b7395","type":"text","text":"* Chart of Accounts\n\t* Balance Sheet\n\t\t*  Assets\n\t\t    *  Current Assets\n\t\t\t\t*  Bank\n\t\t\t\t\t* 1092\n\t\t\t\t\t* 1001 (OP Bank)\n\t\t\t\t\t* 1002 (OP Bank)\n\t\t\t\t\t* so on..\n\t\t\t\t* Accounts Receivable\n\t\t\t\t\t* 1199\n\t\t\t\t\t* 1100\n\t\t\t\t\t* so on..\n\t\t\t\t* Deffered Expense\n\t\t\t\t\t* 1200\n\t\t\t\t\t* 1201\n\t\t\t\t* Other Current Asset\n\t\t\t\t\t* 1099\n\t\t\t* Non current Asset\n\t\t\t\t* Other Asset\n\t\t\t\t\t* 1504\n\t\t\t\t\t* 1505\n\t\t\t\t\t* so on..\n\t\t\t\t* Fixed Asset\n\t\t\t\t\t* Land\n\t\t\t\t\t\t* 1600\n\t\t\t\t\t* building, net\n\t\t\t\t\t\t* 1605\n\t\t\t\t\t\t* 1705\n\t\t\t\t\t* Equipment, net\n\t\t\t\t\t\t* 1610\n\t\t\t\t\t\t* 1710\n\t\t\t\t\t* vehicles, net\n\t\t\t\t\t\t* 1615\n\t\t\t\t\t\t* 1715\n\t\t\t\t\t* furniture & fixtures, net\n\t\t\t\t\t\t* 1620\n\t\t\t\t\t\t* 1720\n\t\t\t\t\t* IT infrastructure & equipment, net \n\t\t\t\t\t\t* 1625\n\t\t\t\t\t\t* 1725\n\t\t\t\t\t* Leasehold improvements, net\n\t\t\t\t\t\t* 1630\n\t\t\t\t\t\t* 1730\n\t\t\t\t\t* construction in progress\n\t\t\t\t\t\t* 1695\n\t\t\t\t\t* fixed asset clearing account\n\t\t\t\t\t\t* 1699\n\t\t* liabilities and equity\n\t\t\t* liabilities\n\t\t\t\t* current liabilities\n\t\t\t\t\t* account payable\n\t\t\t\t\t\t* 2199\n\t\t\t\t\t\t* 2000\n\t\t\t\t\t* credit card\n\t\t\t\t\t\t* 2150\n\t\t\t\t\t* other current liabilities\n\t\t\t\t\t\t* 2001\n\t\t\t\t\t\t* 2002\n\t\t\t\t\t\t* so on...\n\t\t\t\t\t* deffered revenue\n\t\t\t\t\t\t* 2220\n\t\t\t\t\t\t* 2201.1\n\t\t\t\t* long term liability\n\t\t\t\t\t* 2300\n\t\t\t\t\t* 2301\n\t\t\t* Equity\n\t\t\t\t* 3000\n\t\t\t\t* 3002\n\t\t\t\t* so on..\n\t\t\t\t* Member's equity\n\t\t\t\t\t* 3009\n\t\t\t\t\t* so on..\n\t\t\t\t* Retained earnings\n\t\t\t\t\t* Retained Earnings - Current Year Cumulative Income\n\t\t\t\t\t* Retained Earnings - Previous Year Carryforward\n\t\t\t\t\t\t* 3007\n\t\t\t\t\t\t* so on..\n\t* Net income\n\t\t* revenue\n\t\t\t* ticket revenue\n\t\t\t\t* 4000\n\t\t\t\t* 4005\n\t\t\t* sponsorship revenue\n\t\t\t\t* 4100\n\t\t\t\t* so on..\n\t\t\t* food and beverages revenue\n\t\t\t\t* 4200\n\t\t\t\t* 4205\n\t\t\t\t* so on..\n\t\t\t* merchandise revenue\n\t\t\t\t* 4300\n\t\t\t\t* so on..\n\t\t\t* parking revenue\n\t\t\t\t* 4400\n\t\t\t\t* so on..\n\t\t\t* broadcast revenue\n\t\t\t\t* 4500\n\t\t\t\t* 4505\n\t\t\t* nfl revenue\n\t\t\t\t* 4600\n\t\t\t\t* so on..\n\t\t\t* event revenue \n\t\t\t\t* 4700\n\t\t\t\t* so on..\n\t\t\t* cheerleaders revenue\n\t\t\t\t* 4800\n\t\t\t\t* so on..\n\t\t\t* other revenue\n\t\t\t\t* 4900\n\t\t\t\t* so on..\n\t\t\t* foundation contributors\n\t\t\t\t* 4950\n\t\t* expenses\n\t\t\t* salaries and benefits\n\t\t\t\t* player salaries\n\t\t\t\t\t* 5000\n\t\t\t\t\t* so on..\n\t\t\t\t* full time and part time salaries\n\t\t\t\t\t* 5050\n\t\t\t\t\t* so on..\n\t\t\t\t* benefits\n\t\t\t\t\t* 5071\n\t\t\t\t\t* 5072\n\t\t\t\t\t* so on..\n\t\t\t* operating expenses\n\t\t\t\t* travel and entertainment\n\t\t\t\t\t* 5100\n\t\t\t\t\t* so on..\n\t\t\t\t* supplies and services\n\t\t\t\t\t* 5200\n\t\t\t\t\t* 5201\n\t\t\t\t\t* so on..\n\t\t\t\t* football ops expenses\n\t\t\t\t\t* 5300\n\t\t\t\t\t* 5302\n\t\t\t\t* stadium and facilities \n\t\t\t\t\t* 5400\n\t\t\t\t\t* so on..\n\t\t\t\t* sales and marketing \n\t\t\t\t\t* 5517\n\t\t\t\t\t* so on..\n\t\t\t\t* foundation\n\t\t\t\t\t* 5600\n\t\t\t\t\t* so on..\n\t\t\t\t* taxes and insurance\n\t\t\t\t\t* 5700\n\t\t\t\t\t* so on..\n\t\t\t\t* league assessments\n\t\t\t\t\t* 5800\n\t\t\t\t\t* 5801\n\t\t\t\t\t* so on..\n\t\t\t\t* other expense\n\t\t\t\t\t* 5900\n\t\t\t\t\t* so on..\n\t\t\t\t* other income\n\t\t\t\t\t* 6000\n\t\t\t\t\t* so on..\n\t\t\t\t* depreciation expense \n\t\t\t\t\t* 6200\n\t\t\t\t* amortization expense\n\t\t\t\t\t* 6300\n\t\t* other income and expense\n\t\t\t* net interest\n\t\t\t\t* 6100\n\t\t\t\t* so on..\n\t\t\t* gain/loss on sale.\n","x":-12240,"y":11470,"width":960,"height":4450},
		{"id":"a418059972f22867","x":-11280,"y":17180,"width":778,"height":540,"type":"text","text":"### Key observation\n\nOnly the **leaf nodes** (1001–1009, 1092) are **real posting accounts**.\nEverything above them is **structural / grouping only**.\n\nWhat is leaf node?\nLeaf node is a node that has no children. (Posting account)\nWhat is non leaf node?\nA **non-leaf node** is a node that **has one or more children**.\n#### Data Patterns:\n\nPattern 1: Leaf and non-leaf nodes:\n\n```text\nIf member has children → structural\nIf member has no children → posting account\n```\n\n* has_child? Non-leaf node\n* no has_child? leaf - node\n* COA is always joined, never aggregated."},
		{"id":"ef0e3c37b9ae467c","x":-8280,"y":6980,"width":1060,"height":420,"type":"text","text":"|         |                                                    |                                                          |                                    |           |      |            |              |\n| ------- | -------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- | --------- | ---- | ---------- | ------------ |\n| _dim    | _member_name                                       | _member_alias                                            | _parent_name                       | _operator | _cmd | _member_id | _external_id |\n| Account | Balance Sheet                                      |                                                          | Chart of Accounts                  | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | Assets                                             |                                                          | Balance Sheet                      | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | Current Assets                                     |                                                          | Assets                             | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | Bank                                               |                                                          | Current Assets                     | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1092                                               | 1092                                                     | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1001                                               | OP Bank                                                  | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1002                                               | OP Bank                                                  | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1003                                               | OP Bank                                                  | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1004                                               | OP Bank                                                  | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1005                                               | OP Bank                                                  | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1006                                               | kk-bank                                                  | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1007                                               | PNT                                                      | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1008                                               | PNT                                                      | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1009                                               | dependent Bank                                           | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1010                                               | dependent Bank                                           | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1011                                               | OP Bank                                                  | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1012                                               | US Bank                                                  | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1013                                               | US Bank                                                  | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1014                                               | US Bank                                                  | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1015                                               | US Bank                                                  | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1016                                               | US Bank                                                  | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1017                                               | US Bank                                                  | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1018                                               | US Bank                                                  | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1019                                               | US Bank                                                  | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1020                                               | US Bank                                                  | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1021                                               | US Bank                                                  | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1022                                               | US Bank                                                  | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1023                                               | US Bank                                                  | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1024                                               | ENT                                                      | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1025                                               | ENT                                                      | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1026                                               | ENT                                                      | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1027                                               | US Bank                                                  | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1028                                               | US Bank                                                  | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1029                                               | ENT                                                      | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1030                                               | ENT                                                      | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1031                                               | US Bank                                                  | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1032                                               | ENT                                                      | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1033                                               | EN                                                       | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1034                                               | ENT                                                      | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1035                                               | ENT                                                      | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1036                                               | ENT                                                      | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1037                                               | ENT                                                      | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1038                                               | ENT                                                      | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1039                                               | ENT                                                      | Bank                               | +         |      |            |              |\n| Account | 1090                                               | Petty Cash        